CATEGORIES:storytime,library,baby,toddler,family,Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: OCPL - Aliso Viejo Branch\\nCost: free\\nAges: 0-60
  months\\nCategory: Storytime\\n\\nWhat if challenging behaviors are actua
 lly clues? In this interactive workshop\, pediatric occupational speech th
 erapists from Irvine Therapy Services will help parents look beyond meltdo
 wns\, big emotions\, and shutdowns to better understand what may be happen
 ing beneath the surface. Learn how sensory processing\, communication diff
 erences\, and nervous system regulation shape behavior\, and leave with pr
 actical strategies to support your child through connection\, understandin
 g\, and co-regulation.\n\nNo registration required. For more information\,
  email ocpl.programs@occr.ocgov.com or visit ocpl.org/regulation-station\n
 \nThis program is funded by support from the Samueli Foundation.\\n\\nMore
  info: https://ocpl.libcal.com/event/16891575
LOCATION:Aliso Viejo\, Aliso Viejo
URL:https://ocpl.libcal.com/event/16891575
